Flow for 02_node_js from start to end
1. Setup the project
Open 02_node_js
Confirm package.json uses ESM: "type": "module"
scripts include:
npm start → node server.js
npm run dev → node --watch server.js

2. Create the server
server.js:
import http
use import.meta.dirname to get current folder
create server with http.createServer(async (req, res) => { ... })
route requests:
if req.url === '/api':
GET → handleGet(res)
POST → handlePost(req, res)
otherwise → serve static files from public/

3. Build static file handling
utils/serveStatic.js:
resolve public/ folder path
map / to index.html
read the requested file with fs.promises.readFile()
send correct Content-Type
if file missing, return public/404.html
if other error, return 500

4. Add response helper
utils/sendResponse.js:
sets res.statusCode
sets Content-Type
calls res.end(payload)

5. Add content type mapping
utils/getContentType.js:
map extensions like .js, .css, .json, .png, .jpg, .svg
default to text/html

6. Add API route handlers
handlers/routeHandlers.js:
handleGet(res) reads JSON data and returns it
handlePost(req, res) parses JSON body and saves it

7. Parse incoming JSON body
utils/parseJSONbody.js:
collect chunks from req
concatenate them to body
JSON.parse(body)

8. Read and save data
utils/getData.js:
read data/data.json
parse JSON and return it
utils/addNewData.js:
call getData()
push new item
write updated array back to data/data.json

9. Frontend pages and assets
public/
index.html
about.html
contact.html
404.html
index.css
index.js
images/
The contact page uses client-side JavaScript to send form values as JSON to /api

10. Run and test
In terminal inside 02_node_js:
npm install
npm start
Open browser:
http://localhost:8000
Test:
homepage
about page
contact form
invalid path → custom 404
POST form to /api and verify data is written to data/data.json
Summary
This is the full flow:

project setup
server with native http
static file serving
response and content-type helpers
/api GET + POST handlers
request body parsing
data reading/writing
frontend pages
run with npm start